ype {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "First quadrant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f7b15fa-1729-5fc5-b5a4-592994262f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Fourth quadrant" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426887} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e735110-c8f5-5739-8f8c-19b739dad41c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7df69925-7109-5250-8a7b-f9894f0d9138" :question/math-academy-id "q-109032" :question/problem "![](images/69/697a2ef3438aaea021f0886e1172019744c643acc4195daf126e6f64d0a77917.png)\n\nA point $T$ is shown on the axis above. To which quadrant does it belong?" :question/worked-solution "We label the quadrants as follows:\n\n![](images/41/41a419063ce1bc160023de139406c6ed8f66ab4f7046f223386fc5d93dd60292.png)\n\nSince $T$ is placed below and to the right of the origin, it lies in quadrant $\\text{IV},$ which is the fourth quadrant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b509b42a-c38a-5400-8f93-f3e9024b16a2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Coordinates of a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011074f1-cfd6-58bf-a370-02a373de9fcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426865} {:answer/id #uuid "4164de67-68ed-5d58-baf5-fb09924a32e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426891} {:answer/id #uuid "45e3c289-b652-569a-b906-41ad803f5ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426892} {:answer/id #uuid "88d57ad0-69ba-527a-ab06-91ea89cb74df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426909} {:answer/id #uuid "aa17eba7-c7a7-520c-99a2-7d560eb3244c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4164de67-68ed-5d58-baf5-fb09924a32e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426891} :answer-field/id #uuid "073ba61f-9550-5c17-92c4-d58bbcf59d56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "373c04e2-db02-5c16-a78f-083cd4605e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-12470" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d0785d11a903993b04ee55c7fc23f8f219280a45b66df759cbadc1d42fc8c418.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point is $2$ units to the right of the origin, in the positive direction of the $x$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $2.$\n\nAdditionally, the point is $4$ units above the origin, in the positive direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has a $y$-coordinate of $4.$\n\nThe point has an $x$-coordinate of $2$ and a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so its coordinates are $(2,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7fcec0d8-ca03-5446-a42f-65d0ccddd584" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Quadrant of a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2783bd40-3420-50d6-aca2-a036799a1989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426881} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd7f4c1-76d8-526f-9246-9518fbcd5a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426904} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6bb31c-d014-567f-ba52-e3afe3919115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426914} {:answer/id #uuid "a59951d6-4b9c-5418-b347-b1c451db5a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426916} {:answer/id #uuid "dfd571c3-4c79-5b1e-a642-61dd8d70ab4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and  III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a59951d6-4b9c-5418-b347-b1c451db5a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426916} :answer-field/id #uuid "682709b3-961f-5951-9e4b-89301f1f85e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9298397c-357d-5783-87f8-a9a66297312a" :question/math-academy-id "q-169184" :question/problem "![](images/92/928b00ea1ac59e758c4bc9e224d2d27e1c2149e31d0c5c3ab7673ee9abeae208.png)\n\nWhich of the following is true regarding the point $S?$\n\nI. It is in the fourth quadrant\n\nII. Its $x$-coordinate is $1$\n\nIII. Its $y$-coordinate is $-3$" :question/worked-solution "The point $S$ is in the third quadrant, so statement I is false.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the point $S,$ we start at the origin, move $1$ units *left*, and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/f1/f150eac73755dc5f39b499b6ca0ba12624e4c27dd79e7207e11f6c88d04b596d.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,-3).$ Hence, statement II is false and statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5418e0e-fff7-5d08-b915-6e87be27a132" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Point in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df8f4dad-e591-5678-8f1d-eae210ff3731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/2487db2acab8f161c24c07fcf2cdbae330fb372667164ce00b0e84f5656e9327.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052089} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c0e88a-9398-5b02-b421-7ac5a868d034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/53cc8430f8879e8825de16150111d7dc2637e708fb43ca656f69b26e7186ee08.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052090} {:answer/id #uuid "10f50283-9407-568a-a39b-258b584b07cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/77/773973d9e09dfcf7cd09e663951b77d72afc734022f8f0ed96d8ed99be2dce82.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052091} {:answer/id #uuid "1726baca-0423-501f-9dab-a6a81d98de0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3bf3b2abbea979c83d8f7c7f897003c16eb829f2c5bf508b581ff320f8656928.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052092} {:answer/id #uuid "75772131-bfa3-5e36-9673-a06c899c1494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2b/2b5ecad03de381cb38267d7d7d72b55465e0888968b8c3e51c4c98d2fe67bd5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75772131-bfa3-5e36-9673-a06c899c1494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2b/2b5ecad03de381cb38267d7d7d72b55465e0888968b8c3e51c4c98d2fe67bd5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052093} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ccd64d-d574-50ac-bc79-69a45f23bc40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38212f5b-b17b-5e32-8f2c-a84219440404" :question/math-academy-id "q-22344" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the point $C(-2,-3)?$" :question/worked-solution "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units to the *left*, in the negative direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-3,$ so we move $3$ units *down*, in the negative direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](images/e8/e8b3ac34b4fe6c877d606d8ddde5f29c9856cc4bdc5ac14e3ffcf5ddccdc0ebb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5418e0e-fff7-5d08-b915-6e87be27a132" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Point in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bad3df1-27dd-5bde-af42-5f6ef25795ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8b6f66ed603470542d9382226b805f06fb2064e1fe4af2fc964e7fe8fb828283.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426893} {:answer/id #uuid "ac80e56c-e435-5ee8-adb6-3ece38715246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/11/1116f24570e69796a0d12f623cd40646e37989adb8eff39312a3f96c239f016f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426922} {:answer/id #uuid "ac910584-6a41-57c8-ac80-74d776ba44b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/af1e8359640